{{!--
  One drop section: a titled box that accepts Items of a single kind, listing the ones the actor owns
  plus the ones granted by other Items.

  Call it from the root scope of a part template:
    {{> "systems/lotm/templates/actor/player-character/parts/drop-section.hbs"
        zone="abilities" label="LORD_OF_THE_MYSTERIES.Drop.Sections.abilities"
        entries=sections.abilities remove="deleteAbility" add="addAbility"}}

  zone     Key matching DROP_SECTIONS in sheets/actor/sections.mjs (read back from data-drop-zone on drop).
  label    Localization key for the title.
  entries  Array from context.sections.<zone>.
  remove   data-action for the delete button (owned entries only).
  add      Optional data-action for the "+" button.

  Action entries (entry.isAction) get extra fields (buildEntry / addActionButtons in sheets/actor/sections.mjs):
    entry.attack   { label, bonusLabel, tooltip }  the attack button ("Pistol +5"). Empty = no skill set.
    entry.damage   { tooltip }                     the damage button. Empty = no damage formula.
    entry.hasRolls                                 true when there's at least one of the two buttons.
    entry.rangeLabel                               the Range stat ("30 ft", blank when unset).
--}}
<div class="drop-section" data-drop-zone="{{zone}}">
  {{> "systems/lotm/templates/actor/player-character/parts/drop-section-header.hbs" label=label add=add}}

  {{#if entries.length}}
    <ol class="drop-section-list">
      {{#each entries as |entry|}}
        {{> "systems/lotm/templates/actor/player-character/parts/section-entry.hbs" entry remove=../remove}}
      {{/each}}
    </ol>
  {{else}}
    <p class="drop-section-empty">{{localize "LORD_OF_THE_MYSTERIES.Drop.Empty"}}</p>
  {{/if}}
</div>
